HEV -> Boundary : TCP connect to 127.0.0.1:ephemeral
Boundary -> Boundary : accept descriptor; configure socket
alt already stopped / generation retired / pending-authentication full
  Boundary -> Boundary : close descriptor immediately
  note right
    No SOCKS5 method reply and no RFC 1929 reply.
    Never enqueue authentication or hand off to adapter.
  end note
else pending-authentication slot acquired
  Boundary -> Boundary : register pending descriptor\n(M1 captures monotonic deadline at accept)
  HEV -> Boundary : greeting [05 01 02]
  Boundary --> HEV : method selection [05 02]
  HEV -> Boundary : RFC 1929 [01 ULEN UNAME PLEN PASSWD]
  alt wrong/stale capability or M1 absolute deadline expiry
    Boundary --> HEV : [01 01] only when phase and remaining budget permit
    Boundary -> Boundary : close; release pending slot once; no adapter handoff
  else current generation capability
    Boundary --> HEV : [01 00]
    Boundary -> Flow : exclusive HEVSOCKSChannel\npositioned at first request byte
    Flow -> Registry : tryReserve(flow + parser)
    alt adapter capacity unavailable
      Flow --> HEV : bounded REP=01 or close
      Flow -> Registry : release once
    else reserved
      HEV -> Flow : [05 01 00 ATYP DST PORT]\n(+ bounded early payload if coalesced)
      Flow -> Selector : assignment(request) exactly once
      Selector --> Flow : baseline transport + policy
      Flow -> Registry : tryReserve(open)
      Flow -> SSH : openDirectTCPIP(destination,\n127.0.0.1:0, policy)
      alt reject / timeout / cancellation
        SSH --> Flow : stable error or late channel
        Flow -> Channel : close late channel if present
        Flow --> HEV : fixed mapped failure reply when safe
      else channel owned
        SSH --> Flow : SSHByteChannel
        Flow --> HEV : [05 00 00 01 0.0.0.0 0]
        par local to SSH
          loop one bounded local chunk
            HEV -> Flow : partial bytes / EOF
            Flow -> Channel : writeSome prefix / finishWriting
          end
        else SSH to local
          loop one bounded remote chunk
            Channel -> Flow : read bytes / nil EOF
            Flow -> HEV : partial writes / shutdown write half
          end
        end
      end
      Flow -> Flow : first terminal claim; cancel/join pumps
      Flow -> Channel : cancel/reset/close once
      Flow -> Flow : shutdown + close local socket once
      Flow -> Registry : release open/flow/byte reservations once
    end
  end
end

note right of Boundary
  Current source: bounded pending set plus
  per-receive SO_RCVTIMEO inactivity timeout.
  M1: one monotonic accept-to-auth deadline
  spans all reads, comparisons, and replies;
  progress cannot extend it.
end note

note over Selector,Channel
  Selector output is pinned for the flow lifetime.
  M1 performs no lane scheduling; M3 may replace only this seam.
end note

